From: Redmi 7 onclite kernel build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: onclite: allow unsigned modules

Keep module signature verification enabled, but do not require every module
loaded by the Redmi 7 kernel to have a trusted signature. The module loader
continues to reject invalid signatures and all other module checks remain in
place. The selected onc-perf_defconfig is supported by the stock embedded
config and the onclite device-tree BoardConfig reference; it does not prove
the exact MIUI source revision or physical device identity.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/onc-perf_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/onc-perf_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/onc-perf_defconfig
index 0464faefe4cd58d52f511e3cd2dfb5096eb45428..17f3ac12890b1ff11ecc7a5fa16044ad8531f8ca 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/onc-perf_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/onc-perf_defconfig
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 CONFIG_MODULE_FORCE_UNLOAD=y
 CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y
 CONFIG_MODULE_SIG=y
-CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=y
+# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE is not set
 CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_SHA512=y
 # CONFIG_BLK_DEV_BSG is not set
 CONFIG_PARTITION_ADVANCED=y
